<!--
  The small icon Android draws in the status bar and beside the notification.

  It has to be a flat white silhouette on transparency: from Android 5 the
  system takes only the alpha channel and paints it itself, so handing it the
  full-colour launcher icon produces a solid white square — which is what every
  app that skipped this step ships.

  Same path as the logo, so it is recognisably OquNet at 24dp. A vector rather
  than a set of PNGs: it is drawn from the same coordinates as the real mark, it
  scales to every density from one file, and it needed no image tooling.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="700"
    android:viewportHeight="700">
